                                                "example_id": "0e2dd5e4-4126-43d0-9697-38b58f0b0e9a",
                                                "sense_id": "6eef3dcd-15f7-3050-82c8-32a93743cb36",
                                                "text": "For instance, to the extent that living in close proximity to non-white populations entails greater competition for local resources (e.g. jobs, public services) and unequal burden-sharing, one hypothesis predicts that white racial animus increases with the percent of non-whites residing in the local environment (Key, 1949)."
                                            }
